    ('---\nname: architecture-learnings\ndescription: System architecture learnings and common pitfalls to avoid\n---\n\n# Architecture Learnings Skill\n\nReference this skill when encountering system errors or planning architectural changes. Contains documented learnings from past issues.\n\n## Import Structure Fragility\n\n**Issue**: `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named \'bridge\'` when importing `DiscoveryEngine.health_check`\n\n**Cause**: The `DiscoveryEngine` codebase uses implicit relative imports or expects to be run with the `DiscoveryEngine` directory in `sys.path`.\n- `DiscoveryEngine/main.py` imports `bridge` directly (`from bridge.mt5_client...`)\n- `DiscoveryEngine/__init__.py` imports `main`\n- If you import `DiscoveryEngine` as a package from the root, it triggers `__init__`, which loads `main`, which tries to import `bridge`\n\n**Resolution**:\nWhen running scripts from `execution/` that interact with `DiscoveryEngine` internals:\n1. Add project root to `sys.path`\n2. **ALSO** add `DiscoveryEngine/` to `sys.path`\n3. Import modules directly (e.g., `import health_check`) rather than via the package\n\n## Module Shadowing\n\n**Issue**: `AttributeError` when importing `health_check`\n\n**Cause**: `sys.path.append` adds paths to the end. If a standard library or pip-installed package shares the name, it is loaded instead of the local module.\n\n**Resolution**:\n- Use `sys.path.insert(0, path)` to prioritize local modules over site-packages\n- Or rename local modules to be unique (e.g., `discovery_health_check`)\n\n## Key Patterns\n\n### Correct Import Pattern\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Add paths at the FRONT to prioritize local modules\nroot = Path(__file__).parent.parent\nsys.path.insert(0, str(root))\nsys.path.insert(0, str(root / "DiscoveryEngine"))\n\n# Now import directly\nimport health_check\nimport main\n```\n\n### Incorrect Import Pattern\n```python\n# This can fail due to implicit relative imports\nfrom DiscoveryEngine import health_check\n```\n', True),
