    ('---\nname: user-identification\ndescription: Device fingerprinting, machine identification, tiered licensing, and user tracking for Electron desktop apps\nversion: 2.0.0\n---\n\n# User Identification & Licensing Skill\n\nReusable pattern for identifying desktop app users via deterministic hardware fingerprinting, machine ID generation, tiered license management, usage tracking, and paywall gating. Originally implemented in the ExampleApp project.\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\n```\n┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐     ┌──────────────┐\n│  Electron Main   │────▶│  License Server  │────▶│  Turso DB    │\n│  (getHardwareUUID│     │  (Vercel API)    │     │  (SQLite)    │\n│   getMachineId)  │     │                  │     │              │\n└────────┬────────┘     └─────────────────┘     └──────────────┘\n         │ IPC\n┌────────▼────────┐\n│  Renderer/UI     │\n│  (license-store) │\n│  (paywall-dialog)│\n└─────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Layers\n\n| Layer | Purpose | Key Files |\n|-------|---------|-----------|\n| Hardware UUID | Platform-specific hardware identifier | Electron main process |\n| Machine ID | Deterministic SHA-256 hash of UUID + salt | `machine-id.json` cache |\n| Hardware Fingerprint | Secondary dedup hash sent to server | License check request |\n| License Server | Trial/subscription management | Vercel serverless API |\n| License Store | Client-side state + feature gating | Zustand store |\n| Keychain | Machine-specific credential encryption | OS keychain / AES-256-GCM fallback |\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Reference\n\n### 1. Hardware UUID Retrieval\n\nPlatform-specific system identifiers:\n\n```typescript\nimport { execSync } from \'child_process\';\nimport * as fs from \'fs\';\n\nfunction getHardwareUUID(): string | null {\n  try {\n    switch (process.platform) {\n      case \'darwin\': {\n        // macOS: IOPlatformUUID from IORegistry\n        const output = execSync(\n          \'ioreg -d2 -c IOPlatformExpertDevice | grep IOPlatformUUID\',\n          { encoding: \'utf-8\', timeout: 5000 }\n        );\n        const match = output.match(/"IOPlatformUUID"\\s*=\\s*"([^"]+)"/);\n        return match?.[1] || null;\n      }\n      case \'win32\': {\n        // Windows: MachineGuid from registry\n        const output = execSync(\n          \'reg query "HKLM\\\\SOFTWARE\\\\Microsoft\\\\Cryptography" /v MachineGuid\',\n          { encoding: \'utf-8\', timeout: 5000 }\n        );\n        const match = output.match(/MachineGuid\\s+REG_SZ\\s+(.+)/);\n        return match?.[1]?.trim() || null;\n      }\n      case \'linux\': {\n        // Linux: /etc/machine-id or dbus machine-id\n        for (const idPath of [\'/etc/machine-id\', \'/var/lib/dbus/machine-id\']) {\n          try {\n            const id = fs.readFileSync(idPath, \'utf-8\').trim();\n            if (id) return id;\n          } catch { /* try next */ }\n        }\n        return null;\n      }\n      default:\n        return null;\n    }\n  } catch {\n    return null;\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Machine ID Generation\n\nDeterministic ID from hardware UUID, with random fallback:\n\n```typescript\nimport * as crypto from \'crypto\';\nimport * as path from \'path\';\nimport { app } from \'electron\';\n\nconst MACHINE_ID_PATH = path.join(app.getPath(\'userData\'), \'machine-id.json\');\nconst SALT = \'your-app-name-v1\'; // Fixed salt per app\n\nfunction getMachineId(): string {\n  const hwUUID = getHardwareUUID();\n  let machineId: string;\n\n  if (hwUUID) {\n    // Deterministic: same hardware always produces same ID\n    const hash = crypto.createHash(\'sha256\')\n      .update(`${hwUUID}:${SALT}`)\n      .digest(\'hex\')\n      .slice(0, 32);\n    machineId = `mid_${hash}`;\n\n    // Return cached if matches\n    try {\n      if (fs.existsSync(MACHINE_ID_PATH)) {\n        const data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(MACHINE_ID_PATH, \'utf-8\'));\n        if (data.machineId === machineId) return machineId;\n      }\n    } catch { /* ignore */ }\n  } else {\n    // Fallback: use cached random ID or generate new\n    try {\n      if (fs.existsSync(MACHINE_ID_PATH)) {\n        const data = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(MACHINE_ID_PATH, \'utf-8\'));\n        if (data.machineId && typeof data.machineId === \'string\') return data.machineId;\n      }\n    } catch { /* ignore */ }\n\n    machineId = `mid_${crypto.randomBytes(16).toString(\'hex\')}`;\n  }\n\n  // Cache with metadata\n  try {\n    fs.writeFileSync(MACHINE_ID_PATH, JSON.stringify({\n      machineId,\n      hardwareDerived: !!hwUUID,\n      createdAt: new Date().toISOString(),\n    }), { mode: 0o600 });\n  } catch { /* ignore */ }\n\n  return machineId;\n}\n```\n\n**Format**: `mid_` + 32 hex chars (e.g., `mid_a1b2c3d4e5f6...`)\n**Deterministic**: Same hardware always produces the same ID, even if cache is deleted\n**Fallback**: Random bytes if hardware UUID unavailable (persisted once generated)\n\n### 3. Hardware Fingerprint (Anti-Gaming Dedup)\n\nSeparate SHA-256 hash sent to the server to prevent trial abuse across machine IDs:\n\n```typescript\nconst hwUUID = getHardwareUUID();\nconst hardwareFingerprint = hwUUID\n  ? crypto.createHash(\'sha256\').update(`${hwUUID}:${SALT}`).digest(\'hex\')\n  : undefined;\n```\n\n**Format**: 64 hex chars (full SHA-256, vs machine ID\'s 32-char truncation)\n**Purpose**: Server-side deduplication — same hardware can\'t get multiple trials\n\n### 4. License Check Flow\n\n```\nClient                          Server\n  │                               │\n  ├─ POST /api/license-check ────▶│\n  │  { machineId, appVersion,     │\n  │    hardwareFingerprint }      │\n  │                               ├─ Validate machineId format (mid_[a-f0-9]{32})\n  │                               ├─ Lookup license by machineId\n  │                               ├─ If not found: check fingerprint for dedup\n  │                               ├─ If still not found: create 30-day trial\n  │                               ├─ Check trial/subscription expiration\n  │                               ├─ Check revocation status\n  │◀─ { valid, tier, state, ... }─┤\n  │                               │\n  ├─ Cache response locally       │\n  │  (7-day offline grace period) │\n```\n\n### 5. Server-Side Schema (Turso/SQLite)\n\nFour tables managed via `website/lib/db.js`, initialized by `POST /api/init-db` (requires `ADMIN_SECRET`).\n\n#### Users Table (future account system)\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  email TEXT UNIQUE,\n  name TEXT,\n  stripe_customer_id TEXT,          -- Future Stripe integration\n  created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()),\n  updated_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch())\n);\n```\n\n#### Licenses Table\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS licenses (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  user_id TEXT,                      -- FK → users.id (future account linking)\n  machine_id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,   -- Primary identifier\n  hardware_fingerprint TEXT,         -- Deduplication key\n  email TEXT,                        -- Optional registration\n  tier TEXT DEFAULT \'pro\' CHECK (tier IN (\'free\', \'pro\', \'enterprise\')),\n  status TEXT DEFAULT \'active\' CHECK (status IN (\'active\', \'expired\', \'revoked\', \'trial\')),\n  trial_started_at INTEGER,\n  trial_ends_at INTEGER,\n  expires_at INTEGER,\n  created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()),\n  updated_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()),\n  FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(id)\n);\n```\n\n#### License History Table (audit trail)\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS license_history (\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n  license_id TEXT NOT NULL,          -- FK → licenses.id\n  previous_tier TEXT,\n  new_tier TEXT,\n  previous_status TEXT,\n  new_status TEXT,\n  reason TEXT,\n  created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()),\n  FOREIGN KEY (license_id) REFERENCES licenses(id)\n);\n```\n\n#### Usage Events Table (analytics)\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS usage_events (\n  id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n  license_id TEXT,                   -- FK → licenses.id\n  machine_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  event_type TEXT NOT NULL,          -- e.g. \'first_launch\', \'app_launch\', \'fingerprint_dedup\', \'machine_registered\'\n  app_version TEXT,\n  metadata TEXT,                     -- JSON blob\n  created_at INTEGER DEFAULT (unixepoch()),\n  FOREIGN KEY (license_id) REFERENCES licenses(id)\n);\n```\n\n#### Indexes\n\n```sql\nCREATE INDEX idx_licenses_machine_id ON licenses(machine_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_licenses_hardware_fingerprint ON licenses(hardware_fingerprint);\nCREATE INDEX idx_licenses_email ON licenses(email);\nCREATE INDEX idx_licenses_user_id ON licenses(user_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_licenses_status ON licenses(status);\nCREATE INDEX idx_usage_events_machine_id ON usage_events(machine_id);\nCREATE INDEX idx_usage_events_created_at ON usage_events(created_at);\n```\n\n### 6. Machine-Specific Credential Encryption\n\nFor encrypting sensitive data tied to a specific machine:\n\n```typescript\nimport { createHash, createCipheriv, createDecipheriv, randomBytes } from \'crypto\';\nimport { homedir, hostname, platform } from \'os\';\n\nfunction getMachineKey(): Buffer {\n  const machineId = `${hostname()}-${platform()}-${homedir()}`;\n  return createHash(\'sha256\').update(machineId).update(\'your-service-name\').digest();\n}\n\n// Encrypt with AES-256-GCM\nfunction encrypt(data: string): string {\n  const key = getMachineKey();\n  const iv = randomBytes(16);\n  const cipher = createCipheriv(\'aes-256-gcm\', key, iv);\n  let encrypted = cipher.update(data, \'utf8\', \'hex\');\n  encrypted += cipher.final(\'hex\');\n  const authTag = cipher.getAuthTag();\n  return `${iv.toString(\'hex\')}:${authTag.toString(\'hex\')}:${encrypted}`;\n}\n```\n\n**Storage**: OS keychain (keytar) primary, encrypted file fallback\n**Format**: `iv:authTag:ciphertext` (hex-encoded)\n\n### 7. Tier System & Limits\n\n```typescript\n// Global settings from getGlobalSettings() in website/lib/db.js\nconst TIER_CONFIG = {\n  free: {\n    maxAgents: 3,\n    maxFeatures: 25,\n    features: { prioritySupport: false }\n  },\n  pro: {\n    maxAgents: 50,\n    maxFeatures: 100_000,\n    features: { prioritySupport: false }\n  },\n  enterprise: {\n    maxAgents: -1,       // unlimited\n    maxFeatures: -1,     // unlimited\n    features: { prioritySupport: true }\n  }\n};\n```\n\n| Tier | Max Agents | Max Features | Priority Support | Trial |\n|------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|-------|\n| Free | 3 | 25 | No | No |\n| Pro | 50 | 100,000 | No | 30 days (default) |\n| Enterprise | Unlimited (-1) | Unlimited (-1) | Yes | No |\n\n### 8. Machine Registration Endpoint\n\n`POST /api/register-machine` (`website/api/register-machine.js`)\n\n**Request:**\n```json\n{\n  "machineId": "mid_a1b2c3d4...",   // Required, validated: /^mid_[a-f0-9]{32}$/\n  "appVersion": "1.0.0",            // Optional\n  "email": "user@example.com"       // Optional, stored for future account linking\n}\n```\n\n**Response:**\n```json\n{\n  "success": true,\n  "message": "Machine registered successfully",\n  "machineId": "mid_...",\n  "licenseId": "lic_...",\n  "tier": "pro",\n  "status": "trial"\n}\n```\n\n**Flow:**\n1. Validate machineId format\n2. Check if license already exists for this machineId\n3. If not: create new license with `tier: \'pro\'`, `status: \'trial\'`, 30-day trial period\n4. If email provided: update license with email\n5. Log `machine_registered` usage event with `{ hasEmail: boolean }` metadata\n6. Rate limited: 10 req/min per machine\n\n### 9. Client-Side License Store (Zustand)\n\nStore: `apps/ui/src/store/license-store.ts` — persisted as `\'app-license\'`\n\n```typescript\ninterface LicenseStatus {\n  valid: boolean;\n  tier: \'free\' | \'pro\' | \'enterprise\';\n  state: \'active\' | \'trial\' | \'trial_expired\' | \'expired\' | \'revoked\';\n  expiresAt: string | null;\n  features: Record<string, boolean>;\n  message: string | null;\n  gracePeriodDays?: number;\n  limits?: { maxAgents: number; maxFeatures: number };\n}\n```\n\n**Persisted fields:** `license`, `lastChecked`, `machineId`\n**Transient (not persisted):** `paywallOpen`, `paywallReason`\n\n#### Feature Gating Helpers\n\n| Helper | Logic |\n|--------|-------|\n| `canUseFeature(feature)` | Returns false if invalid license; true if enterprise; checks `license.features[feature]` |\n| `canUseModel(model)` | Always true for valid licenses (users bring own API keys) |\n| `isWithinAgentLimit(n)` | Enterprise always true; otherwise `n < maxAgents` (default 1); `-1` = unlimited |\n| `isWithinFeatureLimit(n)` | Enterprise always true; otherwise `n < maxFeatures` (default 5); `-1` = unlimited |\n| `getTier()` | Returns `license?.tier \\|\\| \'free\'` |\n| `getState()` | Returns `license?.state \\|\\| \'active\'` |\n| `isTrial()` | `license?.state === \'trial\'` |\n| `isTrialExpired()` | `license?.state === \'trial_expired\'` |\n\n#### Paywall System\n\n```typescript\n// Open paywall with custom reason\nopenPaywall: (reason?) => set({\n  paywallOpen: true,\n  paywallReason: reason || \'Please upgrade to continue using this feature.\'\n})\n\n// Close paywall\nclosePaywall: () => set({\n  paywallOpen: false,\n  paywallReason: null\n})\n```\n\nThe paywall state is intentionally transient — it resets on page reload so users aren\'t permanently blocked.\n\n#### Development Mode\n\nWhen not running in Electron, the store provides an enterprise-level dev license:\n```typescript\nconst devLicense: LicenseStatus = {\n  valid: true,\n  tier: \'enterprise\',\n  state: \'active\',\n  expiresAt: null,\n  features: {},\n  message: \'Development mode - all features enabled\',\n  limits: { maxAgents: -1, maxFeatures: -1 }\n};\n```\n\n#### Refresh Behavior\n\n- Periodic refresh every 6 hours (21,600,000ms)\n- Only refreshes if: not currently loading AND not offline\n- Cache-Control on server response: `s-maxage=300, stale-while-revalidate=60` (5-min CDN cache)\n\n### 10. Electron IPC Bridge\n\nExposed via `contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld`:\n\n```typescript\nlicense: {\n  get: () => ipcRenderer.invoke(\'license:get\'),\n  refresh: () => ipcRenderer.invoke(\'license:refresh\'),\n  getMachineId: () => ipcRenderer.invoke(\'license:getMachineId\'),\n  register: (email) => ipcRenderer.invoke(\'license:register\', email),\n  onUpdate: (callback) => { /* IPC listener */ },\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Identification Summary\n\n| Type | Format | Derivation | Persistence | Use Case |\n|------|--------|------------|-------------|----------|\n| Hardware UUID | Platform-specific | OS system call | System-level | Source of truth |\n| Machine ID | `mid_[32 hex]` | SHA-256(UUID + salt)[0:32] | Cached file (0o600) | License validation |\n| Hardware Fingerprint | `[64 hex]` | SHA-256(UUID + salt) | Server DB | Trial abuse prevention |\n| Machine Key | 32 bytes | SHA-256(hostname + platform + homedir) | Derived at runtime | Credential encryption |\n\n## Rate Limits\n\n| Endpoint | Limit | Window |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| `/api/license-check` | 30 req | 1 minute |\n| `/api/register-machine` | 10 req | 1 minute |\n\n## Offline Behavior\n\n- License cached locally after each successful check\n- 7-day grace period (configurable) for offline usage\n- Falls open to `free` tier if no cache and no network\n- Periodic refresh every 6 hours when online\n\n## File Locations\n\n| File | Path | Permissions |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| Machine ID cache | `{userData}/machine-id.json` | 0o600 |\n| License cache | `{userData}/license-cache.json` | 0o600 |\n| Encrypted credentials | `{dataDir}/plugin-credentials.enc` | Restricted |\n\n## Fingerprint Deduplication Flow\n\nWhen `/api/license-check` receives a machineId with no existing license:\n\n1. If `hardwareFingerprint` is provided, look up existing license by fingerprint (`getLicenseByFingerprint`)\n2. If found: reuse existing license, update its `machine_id` to the new one\n3. Log `fingerprint_dedup` usage event\n4. If not found: create new 30-day pro trial\n\nThis prevents users from getting multiple trials by reinstalling the app or resetting the machine ID cache.\n\n## License Check Response Format\n\n`POST /api/license-check` returns:\n\n```json\n{\n  "valid": true,\n  "tier": "pro",\n  "state": "trial",\n  "expiresAt": "2026-03-20T00:00:00.000Z",\n  "features": { "prioritySupport": false },\n  "message": null,\n  "gracePeriodDays": 7,\n  "limits": { "maxAgents": 50, "maxFeatures": 100000 }\n}\n```\n\n## Environment Variables\n\n| Variable | Purpose | Default |\n|----------|---------|---------|\n| `TURSO_DATABASE_URL` | Turso database URL | Required |\n| `TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN` | Turso authentication | Required |\n| `ADMIN_SECRET` | Required for `POST /api/init-db` | Required |\n| `FREE_TIER_ENABLED` | Enable/disable free tier | `true` |\n| `TRIAL_DAYS` | Trial duration in days | `30` |\n| `GRACE_PERIOD_DAYS` | Offline grace period | `7` |\n\n## Security Notes\n\n- Hardware UUID never sent raw — always hashed with salt\n- Machine ID uses truncated hash (32 chars) vs fingerprint uses full hash (64 chars)\n- Salt is fixed per app version (`your-app-name-v1`) — update for major versions\n- Credential encryption key derived from machine identifiers (hostname, platform, homedir)\n- File permissions set to owner-only read/write (0o600)\n- Server validates input formats before database operations\n- Email stored on license record but not in usage events (privacy)\n\n## Key File Locations (ExampleApp Project)\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `website/lib/db.js` | Turso client, schema init, `getGlobalSettings()` |\n| `website/api/license-check.js` | License validation endpoint |\n| `website/api/register-machine.js` | Machine registration endpoint |\n| `website/api/init-db.js` | Admin schema initialization endpoint |\n| `apps/ui/src/store/license-store.ts` | Frontend Zustand store, feature gating, paywall |\n| `apps/ui/tests/unit/store/license-store.test.ts` | License store tests |\n| `apps/ui/src/types/electron.d.ts` | Electron API type definitions |\n', True),
